\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dlr Up Vs Yen; Bush Comments Little Help -2-  \b0\par\par\uc2 246 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2004\par 21:04\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2004, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 Nov 22, 2004 (ODC via COMTEX) --  \par \par \uc2 With international meetings over the weekend failing to produce any signs major economies may take concerted action against the dollar's weakness, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  players are now focusing on whether and when Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will act single-handedly to stem further rises in the yen. Japan's Vice Finance Minister for International Affairs Hiroshi Watanabe issued another warning shot to yen bulls Sunday, telling Dow Jones Newswires after the G20 meeting that recent \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  movements "have been rapid and erratic, meaning this is the proper time to think of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." While Watanabe said he didn't have a specific dollar/yen level in mind that would trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , some analysts believe the MOF may step in when the dollar heads for a break of the psychologically important Y100.00 support. "If Bush's remarks (to Koizumi) didn't include the usual U.S. script that markets should decide \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  levels, it could be said that Washington gave tacit approval" to yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out upon a dollar fall below Y100.00, said Yasunari Ueno, chief market economist at Mizuho Securities. Once Tokyo stocks begin to fall on the yen's rise, \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have "justification" to conduct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Ueno said.  \par \par \uc2 -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 -Edited by Hugh Lawson  \par \par \uc2 Copyright 2004 Dow Jones. All rights reserved.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020041122e0bm00262\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
