\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar retreats vs euro in thin trading.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Gertrude Chavez  \par \uc2 602 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2004\par 20:58\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Nov 22 (Reuters) - The dollar fell modestly against the euro on Monday in fairly thin trading, after a meeting of the Group of 20 finance ministers and central bankers in Berlin over the weekend offered no concrete measures to stem the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline.  \par \par \uc2 The G20 communique did not mention \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reinforcing the market's view that the U.S. is willing to tolerate a weaker dollar to ease its burgeoning current account deficit - broadly, a measure of the nation's global trade.  \par \par \uc2 This view gained credence last Friday when Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan warned the deficits were unsustainable and foreign demand for U.S. securities will likely wane.  \par \par \uc2 So although the extent of the dollar's recent losses has forced many dealers to take profit on the euro, adjust positions on the dollar and take a pause in selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the greenback remains on the defensive and close to the lows it touched last week.  \par \par \uc2 "The fundamental factor hurting the dollar was the lack of direction or the lack of concern that the G20 statement conveyed to the market about the the dollar's recent bout of weakness," said Joe Francomano, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Erste Bank in New York.  \par \par \uc2 "The G20 statement overtly went to the extreme of making sure that they did not say anything regarding the dollar. It seems that the benign neglect policy of not only the United States, but also the global community about the dollar's weakness is still in place," he added.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. markets will close on Thursday for the U.S. Thanksgiving holiday, meaning trading this week will be lighter than usual.  \par \par \uc2 In midafternoon trade in New York, the euro was up 0.15 percent at $1.3036 compared with late Friday and close to its record high of $1.3074 reached last week.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was up against the yen at 103.24 yen  but broadly flat\par against the Swiss franc at 1.1628 francs       . Sterling also traded\par little changed against the dollar at $1.8579       .\par   \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 JAPAN INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RISK STILL THERE  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said the G20 policymakers' hands-off approach left the dollar vulnerable to further losses, particularly after Greenspan's speech.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell below 103.00 yen for the first time in over four years after Greenspan's comments and analysts said only the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had stopped it from falling further.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Recent comments from Japanese authorities, suggesting that near-term moves of the dollar against the yen have not been driven by economic fundamentals, underscored the growing risk of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Strong corporate profitability would suggest Japanese firms are better positioned to weather \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  appreciation, but given the recent soft patch of economic data, authorities are likely to be very wary of yen appreciation endangering Japan's recovery, analysts said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Separately, one of the biggest movers of the day was the Canadian dollar which rose to a fresh 12-year high at C$1.1826 against the greenback, according to Reuters data, after bullish comments from the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speaking in Berlin, Bank of Canada Governor David Dodge said the recent rise in the Canadian dollar was "not inappropriate" and that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should only be considered in "extraordinary circumstances".  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "This effectively has the (Canadian) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  do the heavy monetary policy lifting for this \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  as its strengthening is an effective tightening," said Andrew Busch, global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategist at BMO Nesbitt Burns in Chicago.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Additional reporting by Jamie McGeever in New York).   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041122e0bm00ffn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
