\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar dips vs euro - no change to trend post-G20.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Jamie McGeever  \par \uc2 593 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2004\par 18:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK, Nov 22 (Reuters) - The dollar was a touch weaker against the euro on Monday, still under pressure after the meeting in Berlin of Group of 20 finance ministers and central bankers at the weekend failed to signal a policy response to the unit's decline.  \par \par \uc2 The G20 communique did not mention \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , reinforcing the market view that the U.S. is willing to tolerate a weaker dollar to ease its bulging trade and current account deficits.  \par \par \uc2 This view gained credence on Friday when Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan warned the deficits were unsustainable and foreign demand for U.S. securities will likely wane.  \par \par \uc2 So although the extent of the dollar's recent losses has forced many dealers to take profit, adjust positions and take a time out, the greenback remains on the defensive and close to the lows it plumbed last week.  \par \par \uc2 "There's no broad agreement among the central banks on what to do with the dollar, so there's no change," said Patrick Brodie, chief dealer at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking Corporation in New York. "The market's taking a breather here. That might have something to do with the holiday this week, but it still doesn't feel like the dollar's going to get much of a reprieve, even in a thin market."  \par \par \uc2 U.S. markets will close on Thursday for the U.S. Thanksgiving holiday, meaning trading this week will be lighter than usual.  \par \par \uc2 Around noon in New York (1700 GMT), the euro was up 0.2 percent at $1.3041 compared with late Friday and close to its record high of $1.3074 reached last week.   \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The dollar was up a bit at 103.21 yen  but broadly flat at 1.1624 Swiss\par francs       , as was sterling at $1.8583       .\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar index, which is weighted according to daily trading flows against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's main counterparts, was unchanged at 83.14 .  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 INTERVENTION\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  RISK STILL THERE  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Analysts said the G20 policymakers' hands-off approach left the dollar vulnerable, particularly after Greenspan's speech.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell below 103.00 yen for the first time in over four years after his comments and analysts said only the threat of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  was stopping it falling further.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese policymakers have made clear they are unhappy with a stronger yen and recent figures suggest Japan's export-led recovery is already slowing.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui told the Financial Times that yen appreciation could be destabilizing and become a big concern.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Though we do not rule out the possibility of official action to smooth the dollar's decline below 103 yen, there is now increasing risks that officials will come in only when the dollar falls to 100 yen," a JP Morgan research note said Monday.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 One of the biggest movers of the day was the Canadian dollar which rose to a fresh 12-year high against the greenback after bullish comments from the country's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  chief.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Speaking in Berlin, Bank of Canada Governor David Dodge said the recent rise in the Canadian dollar was "not inappropriate" and that \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  should only be considered in "extraordinary circumstances".  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 For \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  traders still keen to sell dollars, Dodge and finance minister Ralph Goodale "made it clear what to buy," said Robert Sinche, head of global \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  strategy at Bank of American in New York.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar fell almost 1 percent to C$1.1826 on Monday, according to Reuters data.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041122e0bm00ctd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
