\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar in sight of low vs euro after G20, Greenspan.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Hideyuki Sano  \par \uc2 746 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2004\par 08:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 22 (Reuters) - The dollar dipped to within sight of another record low against the euro on Monday after a G20 meeting produced no coordinated stance to stem its fall and the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief hinted at more dollar weakness to come.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said that although wariness about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  had curbed losses versus the yen, the dollar was poised to fall further after the Group of 20 rich and developing nations made no reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings in its post-meeting communique on Sunday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was also under pressure after Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan suggested on Friday that a weaker dollar may be needed to help cut the U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 "Although there may not be an explicit policy to drive the dollar down, Greenspan seems to be saying that to solve the U.S. current account problem a fall in the dollar is unavoidable," said Ko Haruki, head of institutional \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at HSBC.  \par \par \uc2 "Naturally that's a pretty good signal to sell the dollar."  \par \par \uc2 As of 0647 GMT the dollar fetched around 103.30 yen , up around 0.2 percent on the day. It was still in sight of the 102.70 yen hit in New York on Friday, the lowest level since March 2000.  \par \par \uc2 The euro bought around $1.3045 , versus 1.3022 in Late U.S. trade.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar touched a record low of $1.3070 per euro on Friday after Greenspan said market appetite for U.S. assets would eventually fall, suggesting foreign capital flows into the United States will become insufficient to fund the gaping deficit.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said that Greenspan's comments, which echoed those of other Fed officials in recent weeks, were the first clear pointer from the Fed chief to a weaker dollar, and would likely accelerate the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's decline.  \par \par \uc2 Some said that another factor supporting the yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the dollar was heightened speculation that China was not far from loosening the yuan's nine-year-old peg against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 A move to revalue the yuan would likely make authorities in Asian countries such as Japan and South Korea more comfortable about allowing their own \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rise against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "We're still looking for a down move in the dollar, and a large part of that is going to have to come against the yen and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , especially if we do see any change in the yuan peg," said Naomi Fink, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst at BNP Paribas.  \par \par \uc2 The G20 communique made no explicit reference to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swings, but it did call for greater exchange rate flexibility in emerging Asian economies.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WATCH  \par \par \uc2 U.S. President George W. Bush reiterated on Sunday his support for a strong dollar, although traders were sceptical, saying that Washington was willing to tolerate a weaker U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "The market thinks the U.S. 'strong dollar' policy is just rhetorical," said Fink at BNP Paribas.  \par \par \uc2 Japan Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said on Monday that he welcomed Bush's reaffirmation of the "strong dollar" policy and said Japan would act against exchange rate volatility.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that in the absence of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would likely soon challenge a 1999 low of 101.25 yen.  \par \par \uc2 Some argued that given the dollar's sharp fall it was increasingly likely that Japan would step into the market to stem the yen's rise and protect the nation's export-led economic recovery.  \par \par \uc2 "With the dollar trading below the bottom marked in March of 103.40, I'd say \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  could take place any time," said Toshihiro Azuma, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  manager at Sumitomo Trust and Banking Corp.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  has not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market since March, after a record 20 trillion yen ($194.1 billion) of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2003.  \par \par \uc2 Some traders said that a sharp drop in Japanese share prices also kept the yen in check.  \par \par \uc2 The Nikkei share average posted its biggest one-day loss in more than three months, falling 2.11 percent to 10,849.39 , as the yen's recent gains raised concerns about the health of Japan's exports.  \par \par \uc2 Bank of Japan Governor Toshihiko Fukui said in an interview published in the Financial Times newspaper that an appreciation in the yen could be destabilising and had the potential to become a "big concern".  \par \par \uc2 (Additional reporting by David McMahon).   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041122e0bm005kz\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
