\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE: Japan Govt Bond Prices Hit 8-Mo High On Yen Rise  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Iain McDonald  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 770 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 November 2004\par 09:44\par \uc2 Dow Jones Capital Markets Report\par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese government bond prices rose to their highest level in eight months Monday due to a surge in the yen, which hit stock prices and boosted expectations that the Bank of Japan's ultra-loose quantitative easing won't end anytime soon.  \par \par \uc2 Some strategists and dealers say bond prices will likely continue to rise in line with any further gains in the yen against the dollar and only yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market will stop the yen's rise and bring to a halt the rally in JGBs.  \par \par \uc2 Still, others say investors are becoming cautious about buying the increasingly expensive JGBs.  \par \par \uc2 The lead December JGB futures contract peaked at 139.02, its highest level since late March, before closing up 0.23 at 138.95.  \par \par \uc2 The surge in prices pushed yields lower across the curve with the yield on the newest five-year JGBs falling two basis points to 0.555%, its lowest level also since late March. The yield on newest 10-year JGBs fell three basis points to 1.40%, its lowest level since Sept. 28.  \par \par \uc2 "Until we define the upper boundary for the exchange rate, I think we're in a grind-higher situation for JGB prices," said John Richards, Japan strategist at Barclays Capital. "But once that ceiling is defined on the yen, then implicitly you also have a ceiling on JGBs as well."  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par       Yen Hits Stocks \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The dollar slumped against the yen Friday to its lowest level since March 2000 after Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan said that "given the size of the U.S. current account deficit, a diminished appetite for adding to dollar balances must occur at some point."  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The greenback held above Y103 for most of the Asian trading session Monday but analysts expect further depreciation.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 The Nikkei 225 Stock Average ended 2.1% lower at 10849.39 and stock analysts say that further yen gains will push stocks further down.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Yen gains against the dollar make Japanese exports more expensive and act as a brake on the economy. This bad news for stocks helps maintain deflationary pressures in Japan and likely means the Bank of Japan will keep its quantitative easing in place for longer than it would have done if the yen had remained stable, analysts said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Though the Nikkei's downside remained solid around 10500 in October and August, "it's possible that the Nikkei may drop below 10500, if the strong yen continues and U.S. stocks keep tumbling," said Toshio Sumitani, a strategist at Tokai Tokyo Research Center.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Investors Wary About Buying Expensive JGBs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 JGB market gains came despite a slide in Treasurys prices indicating that the yen's rise has a much stronger influence on domestic bond prices than a rise in bond prices in the U.S.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Right now, people are transfixed by the stronger yen and what damage it might do to (Japan's) economy," said Barclays' Richards. Barclays estimates that for every 10 yen fall in the dollar, between 0.2% and 0.3% is shaved off the country's gross domestic product.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Strategists say that while JGBs have decoupled from Treasurys and are setting their own course, the two markets will likely recouple again once \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign-exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rates stabilize.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Once the yen steadies, "the recoupling will start," said Richards.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some warn that investors will be reluctant to keep chasing JGB prices higher for fear that any heavy \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  against the yen by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Ministry of Finance\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  will turn the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  around, withdrawing that support from JGB prices.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "The 10-year bond yield may fall below 1.40%, but investors will find it difficult to buy the bonds below that level unless they alter their forecast trading range," said Naomi Hasegawa, senior fixed income strategist at Mitsubishi Securities.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Unless (investors) firmly believe the 10-year bond yield will fall to 1.3% or 1.2%, they won't buy the bonds," she added.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Still, October data from the Japan Securities Dealers Association Monday showed that apart from major banks, most other categories of investors were buyers of JGBs in the first month of the second half of Japan's fiscal year.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Investors bought a net Y1.26 trillion of JGBs, excluding treasury bills, in October after selling a net Y45.6 billion in September.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Iain McDonald, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2941; iain.mcdonald@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 (Hiroshi Inoue, Yoshio Takahashi and Michiyo Seki contributed to this article).  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Hugh Lawson [ 11-22-04 0344ET ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument CM00000020041122e0bm0000d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
