\par\par \b \uc2 JGBs flat near 6-mth highs, BOJ report shrugged off.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By David McMahon  \par \uc2 598 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2004\par 08:20\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 19 (Reuters) - Japanese government bond (JGB) futures prices hovered just below six-month highs on Friday, but the market was barely moved by a Bank of Japan report that said the country's economy may have entered a soft patch.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said although the BOJ's acknowledgement of a slowdown in Japan's economy was mildly supportive for JGBs, the market was having trouble pushing higher because many shared the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's view that the slowdown was temporary.  \par \par \uc2 "If the BOJ proves to be right, because of stronger U.S. data and China not falling out of bed, and Japanese consumption remaining robust, the economy is set to bounce and not continue down a negative track," said John Richards, Japan strategist at Barclays Capital.  \par \par \uc2 Richards said that would mean JGB yields had little room to fall and would probably start climbing again soon.  \par \par \uc2 The BOJ said in its monthly economic report on Thursday that although Japan's economy was continuing its recovery on the whole, it was suffering from a "short-term lull in exports and output".  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts think the bond market has already factored in a soft patch in Japan's economy, with the benchmark 10-year yield down around 50 basis points from a four-year high of 1.94 percent scaled in June.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that with no major economic data in Japan due until consumer prices on Nov. 26, and no long-bond auctions set for the rest of the month, many investors were taking a breather.  \par \par \uc2 "Especially with a holiday next week and no big events, a lot of investors are thinking it's OK just to sit on their portfolios until something happens," said Makoto Suzuki, head of fixed-income sales at ABN Amro.  \par \par \uc2 "Business is very quiet today."  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year yield ended the day unchanged at 1.430 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year futures contract edged up 0.08 point to 138.72. It hit 138.79, the highest since May 27, on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese financial markets will be closed on Tuesday for a national holiday.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  WATCH  \par \par \uc2 The yen's climb to a 7-1/2-month peak of 103.8 per dollar on Wednesday raised worries that exports, a main driver of the economy, would become more expensive, hurting economic growth.  \par \par \uc2 JGB prices could continue to edge up with any further gains in the yen, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The market will be closely watching a meeting of G20 finance ministers later on Friday for any signs of a coordinated stand to help stem sharp falls in the dollar, which hit a record low against the euro on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Most dealers do not expect the meeting to herald any coordinated \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy.  \par \par \uc2 The sharp rise in the yen added to worries already compounded by data last Friday that showed Japan's economy grew by an unexpectedly sluggish 0.3 percent on an annualised basis in July-September, dragged down by slowing exports to the United States and China and weak capital spending.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said investors were looking out for any dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as such a move could halt the rise in the yen and hurt JGB prices by diminishing expectations of a slowdown in exports.  \par \par \uc2 "If you bought JGBs on the expectation that the dollar is going to go towards 95 yen, and the BOJ says, 'No it isn't', then maybe you're not going to want to own those bonds any more," said Barclays' Richards.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041119e0bj006py\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
