\par\par \b \uc2 Japan Tanigaki: To Take Resolute Action In  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2  If Needed  \b0\par\par\uc2 418 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2004\par 01:43\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    TOKYO (Dow Jones)--Japanese Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki said Friday that while the yen appears to have come down slightly off recent highs against the dollar, current market conditions still require close monitoring.   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "While I won't comment on specific \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  levels, current conditions need to be watched with great caution," Tanigaki told reporters.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 "If there is a need to, we will resolutely do what we have to do," Tanigaki said, referring to the possibility \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets if it feels that movements are too rapid or speculative, and have strayed too far from economic fundamentals.  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki was speaking after the dollar fell to a seven-month low of Y103.65 Thursday. As of 0102 GMT, it was trading at Y104.26. [ 19-11-04 0103GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Tanigaki also repeated that he believes the economy has recovered enough to consider reducing and abolishing past income tax cuts, as the economy is finally "nearing an exit" from prolonged stagnation after the burst of Japan's asset-inflated bubble economy in the early 1990s.  \par \par \uc2 "We have finally overcome the bad-loan problem," which had been the cause of many setbacks suffered by past economic recoveries, Tanigaki said, pointing out that major banks have made great progress in purging non-performing loans from their balance sheets.  \par \par \uc2 And while Tanigaki acknowledged that changes to gross domestic product calculation methods have pushed down past GDP figures, he said the government was looking at the economy not only through GDP, but through a variety of indicators.  \par \par \uc2 The revisions "aren't necessarily going to change our view," he said. "Overall, the economy remains in a private sector demand-led recovery."  \par \par \uc2 The Cabinet Office said Thursday it will revise the method for calculating real GDP to better reflect economic reality, beginning with revised data for July-September GDP, due Dec. 8.  \par \par \uc2 The government will change the way it measures price changes through the GDP deflator, by updating the reference year for price decline calculations on an annual basis, as opposed to once every five years under the current formula.  \par \par \uc2 If the new method had been used for past data, it would have resulted in a 0.1% contraction in annualized real GDP for the July-September, and not the 0.3% expansion initially reported.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Miyako Takebe, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; miyako.takebe@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Chris Gallagher and Kirsty Mackenzie [ 19-11-04 0146GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041119e0bj0000o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
