\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Dollar Hits Year Low Against Yen As Greenspan Speaks  \b0\par\par\uc2 302 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 November 2004\par 15:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2004, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 New York (Dow Jones)--The dollar reached a low for 2004 versus the yen in early New York trading Friday, as traders used remarks by Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan as an excuse to sell the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar fell to Y103.18, crashing through the previous low for the year of Y103.43 reached in late March. The yen was at Y104.19 late Thursday in New York.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's fall also left the euro near a fresh all-time high amid broad losses for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The euro is at $1.3052, though it reached as high as $1.3067, from $1.2959 late Thursday. That's just off the $1.3074 high it reached in Asian trading early Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 At 9.00 a.m. EST (1400 GMT), the dollar was fetching CHF1.1596, from CHF1.1626 late Thursday, while the pound was at $1.8598 against $1.8506.  \par \par \uc2 After weakening overnight, the dollar dipped sharply once Greenspan's speech to a conference of European bankers in Berlin was released. According to traders, there's nothing immediately obvious in the text of Greenspan's speech to serve as a trigger for a selloff.  \par \par \uc2 His comments actually downplayed concerns about the U.S. current account deficit, saying there's no evidence that the gap is hard to finance. Greenspan also said that reducing budget deficit will lower risk of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis. Greenspan doesn't believe such a crisis is pre-ordained.  \par \par \uc2 Greenspan is appearing along with European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Jean-Claude Trichet.  \par \par \uc2 There has been some speculation among traders that a new year high for the yen may trigger \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  on behalf of the Japanese government. The BOJ last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March.  \par \par \uc2 - -   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020041119e0bj008et\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
