\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Stays Weak Vs Yen, Euro; No BOJ Action  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 831 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2004\par 06:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar remained weak against the yen and euro in Asian trading Thursday after plunging overnight, as traders figured \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  anytime soon to push down the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 "Sentiment is 'sell the dollar.' The only positions the market is creating are dollar-short positions," said Mitsuo Imaizumi, deputy general manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Daiwa Securities SMBC.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. hedge funds and other speculators dragged down the dollar to as low as Y103.85 in the session amid expectations that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't order \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls to Y103.00, or even Y100.00, traders said. Selling by some Japanese exporters weighed on the dollar too, they said.  \par \par \uc2 The euro also stayed close to its all-time high of $1.3047, but didn't break through that level in Asian trading because of Japanese exporters' selling of euros for yen kept the euro from rising against the dollar as well, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Japanese officials continued to warn Thursday they might take action against the yen's steep rise against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "I'm concerned about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  (levels) and they need to be watched very closely," said Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki.  \par \par \uc2 But traders said they doubt Tokyo officials will follow up their words with action, at least for the time being.  \par \par \uc2 "There's still plenty of room for further dollar declines" in the dollar against the yen, and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the dollar falls below Y103.00, said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JPMorgan Chase Bank in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 23:50 EST / 0450 GMT \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Low 12/31  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par USD/JPY Yen              103.95-97  104.02-07  -0.07  104.12  103.85   -3.16 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.3034-39  1.3031-34  +0.02  1.3043  1.3028   +3.48 \par GBP/USD Sterling         1.8594-02  1.8593-98  +0.01  1.8606  1.8585   +4.09 \par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      1.1625-63  1.1629-33  -0.03  1.1639  1.1616   -6.22 \par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     1.1929-35  1.1944-46  -0.13  1.1949  1.1925   -8.19 \par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   0.7818-22  0.7813-17  +0.06  0.7823  0.7807   +3.80 \par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.7075-85  0.7076-81  -0.01  0.7087  0.7070   +8.02 \par USD/DEM Deutsche Mark    2.2150-75  2.2150-75   0.00  2.2157  2.2160   -0.11 \par Euro Rates \par EUR/JPY Yen              135.52-55  135.57-64  -0.04  135.73  135.36   +0.29 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 18-11-04 0556GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Later in the session, the dollar fell to a new seven-month low at Y103.62 on speculative selling, while the euro rose to a fresh record high at $1.3068.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "As a short-term trader, I was very encouraged by falls in the euro and other majors" against the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , as the drops suggest \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  may not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  because it would be hard to boost the dollar against the yen when it is weakening against many other \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , a dealer at a Japanese bank said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 During London trading hours Thursday, players might try to push down the U.S. \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to a four-and-a-half-year low of Y103.00, and might try to lift the euro to $1.3100, he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  officials know that because the current dollar-weakness is most pronounced against the euro, there's not much they can do, said Atsushi Mizuno, chief strategist at Credit Suisse First Boston in Tokyo.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Also, "the new stance of Japan's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  authorities may be to not react excessively against \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market volatility," he said. "In the long run, (that) will contribute to maintaining stability" in the dollar/yen exchange rate, he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Some analysts also said Tokyo might not \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of a Group of 20 finance authorities' meeting scheduled in Berlin from Friday.  \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  has historically been "very unwilling to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  ahead of international gatherings" such as the weekend G20 meeting, Morgan Stanley said in a research note.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 To be sure, not everyone is off guard against Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 BNP Paribas analysts said the speed of the dollar's recent declines against the yen has been raising concern over chances of Japanese \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , and that they "would not be surprised if there were (seen or unseen) official actions" to prop up the dollar.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But they added that even if \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Japan\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's MOF \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervenes\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to boost the dollar, it will "simply provide a better selling level" in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par    -By Takashi Nakamichi, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; takashi.nakamichi@dowjones.com \par  \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 18-11-04 0715GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041118e0bi0006j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
