\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Stays Weak Vs Yen, Euro; No BOJ Action  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Takashi Nakamichi  \par \uc2 493 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 November 2004\par 21:04\par \uc2 OsterDowJones Commodity Wire\par \uc2 OSTDJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2004, Comtex News Network.  All Rights Reserved.  Standard Attribution Statement: News Provided by COMTEX.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO, Nov 18, 2004 (ODC via COMTEX) --  \par \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \par \uc2 The dollar remained weak against the yen and euro in Asian trading Thursday after plunging overnight, as traders figured \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  anytime soon to push down the Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "Sentiment is 'sell the dollar.' The only positions the market is creating are dollar-short positions," said Mitsuo Imaizumi, deputy general manager of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Daiwa Securities SMBC. U.S. hedge funds and other speculators dragged down the dollar to as low as Y103.85 in the session amid expectations that \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  won't order \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  falls to Y103.00, or even Y100.00, traders said. Selling by some Japanese exporters weighed on the dollar too, they said. The euro also stayed close to its all-time high of $1.3047, but didn't break through that level in Asian trading because of Japanese exporters' selling of euros for yen kept the euro from rising against the dollar as well, traders said. Japanese officials continued to warn Thursday they might take action against the yen's steep rise against the dollar. "I'm concerned about \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  (levels) and they need to be watched very closely," said Finance Minister Sadakazu Tanigaki. But traders said they doubt Tokyo officials will follow up their words with action, at least for the time being. "There's still plenty of room for further dollar declines" in the dollar against the yen, and the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  until the dollar falls below Y103.00, said Tohru Sasaki, chief \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at JPMorgan Chase Bank in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 23:50 EST / 0450 GMT\par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg\par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High\par   Low 12/31\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/JPY Yen              103.95-97  104.02-07  -0.07  104.12  103.85   -3.16\par EUR/USD Euro             1.3034-39  1.3031-34  +0.02  1.3043  1.3028   +3.48\par GBP/USD Sterling         1.8594-02  1.8593-98  +0.01  1.8606  1.8585   +4.09\par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      1.1625-63  1.1629-33  -0.03  1.1639  1.1616   -6.22\par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     1.1929-35  1.1944-46  -0.13  1.1949  1.1925   -8.19\par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   0.7818-22  0.7813-17  +0.06  0.7823  0.7807   +3.80\par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.7075-85  0.7076-81  -0.01  0.7087  0.7070   +8.02\par USD/DEM Deutsche Mark    2.2150-75  2.2150-75   0.00  2.2157  2.2160   -0.11\par Euro Rates\par EUR/JPY Yen              135.52-55  135.57-64  -0.04  135.73  135.36   +0.29\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Copyright 2004 Dow Jones. All rights reserved.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument OSTDJ00020041118e0bi000d1\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
