\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 : Dollar Flat Vs Yen, Euro; Outlook Still Weak  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Leika Kihara  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 707 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2004\par 06:22\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 TOKYO (Dow Jones)--The dollar was largely flat against the yen and the euro in Asia Wednesday, as the greenback's recent resilience prompted dollar bears to wait for fresh cues to drive it down further.  \par \par \uc2 While market players generally agree that the dollar's long-term outlook remains weak, bids by players covering short positions and those defending option triggers at Y105.00 gave the U.S. unit firm support, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The greenback also showed resilience against the euro as players were reluctant to bid up the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , knowing that profit-taking and option-related offers were providing tough resistance at $1.30, they said.  \par \par \uc2 "The trend is to sell dollars and that's decided," said Noriyuki Fujita, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales at Societe Generale's Tokyo branch.  \par \par \uc2 "Traders are just waiting for a push in the back" to resume aggressive dollar selling, such as dollar-bearish comments from finance ministers and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governors attending the G-20 meeting in Berlin later this week, Fujita said.  \par \par \uc2 Many analysts still hold the view that the dollar's break below the psychologically important Y105.00 mark is only a matter of time, but the U.S. unit's recent resilience is making some dollar bears nervous.  \par \par \uc2 "I don't think it's yen-selling \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  (by \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) but there seem to be steady dollar bids above Y105.00," said a trader at a Tokyo-based U.S. bank.  \par \par \uc2 Dollar bears may wait a while before pushing the greenback lower, as the euro's rise and the dollar's drop have made the yen and the euro vulnerable to profit-taking, the trader said.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par Interbank \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Foreign Exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  Rates At 00:50 EDT / 0450 GMT \par  \par                          Latest     Previous   %Chg   Daily   Daily    %Chg \par Dollar Rates                        2150 GMT          High \par    Low      12/31 \par  \par USD/JPY Yen              105.40-43  105.33-36  +0.07  105.53  105.32   -1.81 \par EUR/USD Euro             1.2958-62  1.2956-58  +0.02  1.2965  1.2950   +2.87 \par GBP/USD Sterling         1.8527-31  1.8530-33  -0.02  1.8543  1.8518   +3.72 \par USD/CHF Swiss Franc      1.1746-51  1.1759-65  -0.11  1.1767  1.1748   -5.24 \par USD/CAD Canadian Dlr     1.1946-51  1.1962-68  -0.13  1.1966  1.1942   -8.06 \par AUD/USD Australian Dlr   0.7731-36  0.7723-26  +0.10  0.7733  0.7722   +2.64 \par NZD/USD New Zealand Dlr  0.7003-13  0.6989-97  +0.20  0.7008  0.6986   +6.92 \par USD/DEM Deutsche Mark    2.2150-75  2.2150-75   0.00  2.2157  2.2160   -0.11 \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 17-11-04 0522GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Many players don't expect much \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  market reaction from a slew of U.S. economic indicators due out later in the day, including the October consumer price index, housing starts and industrial production.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Concern over the huge U.S. current account deficit instead will continue to take center stage and weigh on the dollar, traders said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Despite Tuesday's U.S. Treasury International Capital System, or TICS, data showing the nation attracted enough inflow of funds in September to cover its trade gap, the U.S. deficit "will remain a problem in the current environment" and continue to pressure dollar/yen lower in the medium-term, analysts at BNP Paribas said in a research note.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 But not all players are convinced that once the dollar slips below Y105.00, it won't find much support until it reaches this year's low of Y103.40.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Those who wanted to build dollar/yen positions have already done so, but there are still players waiting to sell dollars above Y106.00 and buy below Y105.00," Societe Generale's Fujita said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 "Dollar bids below Y105.00 look quite thick, so even if the greenback fell below Y105.00, it probably won't go straight down to Y103.40," he said.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Bennett Richardson [ 17-11-04 0638GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1074  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041117e0bh0006g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
