\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Weaker dollar turns back towards lows.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Carolyn Cohn  \par \uc2 671 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 November 2004\par 10:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Nov 12 (Reuters) - The dollar fell half a percent against the yen to within sight of seven-month lows and edged towards recent record lows against the euro on Friday as worries persisted about the U.S. current account deficit.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar has lost as much as five percent against the yen and six percent against the euro since early October, as markets fretted the U.S. would fail to attract sufficient investor flows to plug its huge current account gap.  \par \par \uc2 Recent speculation in U.S. and Japanese newspapers that the U.S. administration will tolerate a weaker dollar was boosting \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday, with wariness of further verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from euro zone policymakers keeping the euro in check.  \par \par \uc2 "We have had a bit of profit-taking, but Trichet's comments have had less impact on the euro than in January," said Trevor Dinmore, \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank.  \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. election has removed uncertainty about the U.S. dollar policy, and markets are expecting four more years of benign neglect."  \par \par \uc2 The dollar bought around 106 yen at 0845 GMT, compared with 106.63 in late trade in New York, where movements were thin due to the Veterans Day holiday. There was also some talk of dollar sales ahead of U.S. Treasury coupon repayments on Monday. A fall through 105.23 would take the dollar to seven-month lows.  \par \par \uc2 The euro fetched 136.95 yen, compared with 137.63, down a third of a percent from the U.S. close.  \par \par \uc2 The euro was at $1.2920, slightly up from late U.S. trade, after hitting a record high of $1.3005 on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar was at 84 against an index of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a little above recent nine-year lows.  \par \par \uc2 U.S. retail sales data for October at 1330 GMT are forecast to show a rise of 0.2 percent, from a 1.5 percent gain in September.  \par \par \uc2 The University of Michigan preliminary sentiment survey for November is due at 1445 GMT and forecast to show a rise to 93.0 from 91.7 in October.  \par \par \uc2 EURO CAPPED  \par \par \uc2 The euro was capped as a chorus of comments from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policymakers helped the dollar's cause.  \par \par \uc2 ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet said on Thursday he stood by a statement he made on Monday in which he described recent euro/dollar movements as "brutal", while colleagues expressed concerns about the pace of the euro's recent gains.  \par \par \uc2 Similar "brutal" remarks by Trichet in January took more than three percent off the value of the euro in less than a week, while this week the euro was trading only a little below Monday's opening levels.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said they were confident the ECB would limit \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the verbal kind for the time being.  \par \par \uc2 "So long as there is two-way trading - and there has been some selling in the euro - (verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) probably suits the ECB's goal of keeping volatility manageable," said Naomi Fink, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at BNP Paribas in Tokyo.  \par \par \uc2 Third quarter growth data for the euro zone is due at 1000 GMT, forecast to show growth of 0.3 percent. ECB executive council member Gertrude Tumpel-Gugerell is expected to give a speech during the European morning.  \par \par \uc2 JAPAN GROWTH  \par \par \uc2 The yen quickly recovered losses in Tokyo made after data showing Japan's economy grew a real 0.1 percent in July-September from the previous quarter. That was below economists' forecasts for growth of 0.5 percent.  \par \par \uc2 The yen was also finding support from speculation over whether and when China would alter its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  regime, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 China's yuan trades in a narrow range at around 8.28 to the dollar, but it is widely believed to be undervalued and helping Chinese exporters.  \par \par \uc2 Beijing has come under pressure, particularly from Washington, to adopt a more flexible \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  system.  \par \par \uc2 Such a revaluation would likely support the yen and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041112e0bc00akw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
47
