\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 FOREX \highlight\uc2 -Dollar bobs near fresh record low against euro.  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Christina Fincher  \par \uc2 707 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2004\par 14:27\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Nov 8 (Reuters) - The dollar hit a fresh record low against the euro and a nine-year low on a trade-weighted index on Monday as investors continued to shun the greenback on worries over the United States' bloated deficits.  \par \par \uc2 A warning on \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  moves from the head of the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  gave the dollar some respite but many analysts said it was only a matter of time before the greenback hit the psychological $1.30 level.  \par \par \uc2 Speaking following a meeting of top central bankers in Basel, ECB President Jean-Claude Trichet said the euro's recent climb against the dollar was "not welcome" and "brutal" - comments which echoed those made the last time the euro hit a record high in February.  \par \par \uc2 "Trichet is trying to repeat the trick he pulled off earlier this year but I am not sure he is going to be able to pull it off this time," said Ian Gunner, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  research at Mellon Financial.  \par \par \uc2 Gunner added the dollar's fall was still in its infancy and investors needed to see a move towards $1.34 in the euro before they would be willing to take profits.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar stood at $1.2920 per euro at 1312 GMT, having earlier hit an all-time low at $1.2985. It fetched 105.65 yen, having earlier fallen to its lowest since April at 105.30 yen.  \par \par \uc2 WHERE NEXT?  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's weakness was broad based with the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hitting a nine-year low against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  below 83.80, a 12-year low against the Canadian dollar and an 8-year low against the Swiss franc.  \par \par \uc2 "The U.S. has a current account deficit, a budget deficit and a president who appears unconcerned about dollar weakness," said Shahab Jalinoos, senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at ABN AMRO. "No one can see any reason to buy the dollar at the moment."  \par \par \uc2 The latest bout of dollar weakness began in the middle of last week as investors took the view the administration of re-elected President George W. Bush would do little to alleviate the country's structural problems.  \par \par \uc2 The budget deficit is about $427 billion, or 3.7 percent of gross domestic product, while the current account, the broadest measure of trade, hit a record $166.18 billion shortfall in the second quarter.  \par \par \uc2 Even Friday's stronger-than-expected U.S. employment report failed to lift the dollar's gloom for long.  \par \par \uc2 "The big issue is what does the U.S. election mean for dollar policy," said Karmal Sharma, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwort Wasserstein. "The previous one was of benign neglect and most people think that the weaker dollar will continue."  \par \par \uc2 PAIN THRESHOLD?  \par \par \uc2 Top central bankers meeting in Basel said on Sunday they were keeping a wary eye on \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but analysts said Japanese and euro zone policymakers were unlikely to step into the market to stop the dollar's fall at this stage.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily on the foreign exchanges, selling about 35 trillion yen ($332.2 billion) in 2003 through to March this year. But analysts say Tokyo is unlikely to repeat such a large scale campaign given the Japanese economy is now in better shape.  \par \par \uc2 Euro zone policymakers have also sounded fairly relaxed about recent exchange rate moves, noting a weaker dollar helps to combat inflation and cushion the impact of high oil prices.  \par \par \uc2 ECB Chief Economist Otmar Issing declined on Monday to comment on the euro's exchange rate, while Germany's DIHK chambers of trade and industry said the euro would not threaten Germany's 2005 growth prospects unless it rose above $1.30 for a "lasting" period.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar's best chance of a rebound in the near term is after the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy meeting on Wednesday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The market has already priced in a quarter-point U.S. rate rise this month but is less certain about a hike in December. If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  indicates it will raise rates again next month, that could help the dollar, as higher rates are likely to draw more foreign capital into the United States.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020041108e0b800hd3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
