\par\par \b \uc2 Asia  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2 :Dollar Rises As Shorts Covered Pre-Election-2-  \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 November 2004\par 07:24\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 Data released Monday showed speculators' net yen-long positions soared to 27,636 contracts in the week to Oct. 26 from 8,565 contracts the week before. It was the largest volume of yen longs since the week to Feb. 17, so the unwinding of these positions may briefly send the dollar higher.  \par \par \uc2 That has led J.P. Morgan Chase Bank of Tokyo to recommend unwinding dollar-short, yen-long positions for now and begin selling the U.S. unit again when it bounces back above Y107.00.  \par \par \uc2 "In the medium- to long-term, our expectations for a weaker dollar haven't changed, but given the recent buildup of yen longs and the events calendar this week, we recommend buying back shorts," said Tohru Sasaki, the bank's chief \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist.  \par \par \uc2 The dollar, however, likely won't find much support other than such position-adjustment, with little chance for Japan's \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  to step into the market to stem the yen's rise at current levels, traders say.  \par \par \uc2 "With an end to \b \highlight22\uc2 Japan\b0 \highlight\uc2 's deflation in sight, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if there is any, will come below Y105.00," said Daisuke Uno, market analyst at Sumitomo Mitsui Banking, noting that the chance of MOF action will increase only when the dollar falls below its March 31 low of Y103.40.  \par \par \uc2 Uno expects the dollar to test its Feb. 11 low of Y105.16 this week and target Y100-Y105 by the end of this year.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par    -By Leika Kihara, Dow Jones Newswires; 813-5255-2929; leika.kihara@dowjones.com \par    -Edited by Hugh Lawson \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 [ 01-11-04 0624GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020041101e0b10006l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
